; ============================================================================
; Appendix D: Formal ABNF Grammar for the cdcf: URI Scheme
; draft-cdcf-catholic-uri-scheme-04 · version 0.5.0, with unreleased [REV-05]
; changes
;
; This grammar is NORMATIVE. Any cdcf: identifier that does not conform to
; these productions is invalid. Implementations MUST reject non-conforming
; identifiers. Future domains introduced by sub-specifications MUST extend
; this grammar via a release of the main specification, following the
; grammar revision process in spec/06-governance.md §6.6. [REV-05]
;
; Notation per RFC 5234 (https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5234).
;
; Changes since 0.3.0:
;   [REV-03] concept-path is an opaque CN-prefixed ID, not a slug (§3.5)
;   [REV-03] osis-book must be the exact lower-cased OSIS 2.1.1 book ID
;   [REV-04] "person" domain and person-path withdrawn (§3.6.1)
;   [REV-04] "work" domain and work-path added (§3.6)
;   [REV-04] concept-path prefix written as a case-sensitive hex literal
;   [REV-04] papal issuer-slug ordinal only where part of the official name
;   [REV-05] cdcf-id binds each path production to its own domain; the
;            "domain" rule and the incremental "domain-path =/" alternatives
;            (which had no initial "=" definition) are removed
;   [REV-05] concept-num: at least four digits, no extra leading zeros
;   [REV-05] work-path separates sub-division segments with SLASH (the
;            0.3.0–0.5.0 form "[SLASH 1*path-segment]" omitted the separator)
;   [REV-05] controlled vocabularies (code, inst-type, rel-slug) are "slug";
;            their values are registered, not part of the grammar (§6.6)
; ============================================================================

; ── Core character classes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
ALPHA    = %x61-7A                          ; a-z (lower-case only)
DIGIT    = %x30-39                          ; 0-9
HYPHEN   = %x2D                             ; -
SLASH    = %x2F                             ; /
slug     = 1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / HYPHEN)       ; general-purpose slug
roman    = 1*(%x69 / %x76 / %x78 / %x6C / %x63 / %x64 / %x6D)
                                             ; i v x l c d m (Roman numerals)
iso-date = 4DIGIT HYPHEN 2DIGIT HYPHEN 2DIGIT  ; YYYY-MM-DD

; ── Top-level production ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; A cdcf: identifier is a domain name followed by a slash and the path form
; of THAT domain. [REV-05] Binding each path to its domain makes
; e.g. "ccc/summa-theologiae" invalid; a new domain adds one alternative here.
cdcf-id  = "verse"       SLASH verse-path
         / "book"        SLASH book-path
         / "magisterium" SLASH magisterium-path
         / "ccc"         SLASH ccc-path
         / "canon"       SLASH canon-path
         / "concept"     SLASH concept-path
         / "work"        SLASH work-path
         / "institution" SLASH institution-path
         / "rel"         SLASH rel-path

; ── Scripture ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
book-path    = osis-book
verse-path   = osis-book SLASH chapter [SLASH verse-ref]
osis-book    = slug                          ; the exact lower-cased OSIS 2.1.1 book ID
                                             ; (e.g. "john", not "jn")
chapter      = 1*DIGIT
verse-ref    = 1*DIGIT [HYPHEN 1*DIGIT]      ; single verse or range

; ── Magisterium ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
magisterium-path = issuer-slug SLASH doc-slug [SLASH section-type SLASH section-id]
issuer-slug      = slug                      ; council, dicastery, or pope-{name}[-{roman}]
                                             ; (§3.2.3)
doc-slug         = slug                      ; ASCII-folded official title or incipit
                                             ; (§3.2.4)
section-type     = "chapter" / "canon" / "paragraph" / "article"
section-id       = 1*DIGIT

; ── Catechism ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ccc-path    = para-num [HYPHEN para-num]
para-num    = 1*DIGIT

; ── Canon Law ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
canon-path  = code SLASH canon-num [SLASH canon-qualifier]
code        = slug                          ; a registered code of canon law
                                             ; (§3.4.1); [REV-05] formerly an
                                             ; enumeration in this grammar
canon-num   = 1*DIGIT
canon-qualifier = para-num                  ; paragraph number — always numeric
              / "authentic-interpretation" SLASH iso-date
                                             ; fixed keyword + ISO date — unambiguous

; ── Theological Concepts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
concept-path = %x43.4E concept-num           ; "CN", case-sensitive; opaque,
                                             ; semantics-free (see §2.6)
concept-num  = 4DIGIT / %x31-39 4*7DIGIT     ; [REV-05] 0001–9999 zero-padded to
                                             ; four digits; 10000 upward with no
                                             ; leading zero (§3.5.1)
; concept-notation = slug                    ; skos:notation mnemonic; NOT a URI
;                                            ; path segment

; ── Works ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
work-path     = work-slug *(SLASH path-segment) ; [REV-05] slash-separated
work-slug     = slug                        ; registry-unique; author-qualified
                                             ; where a title is shared
path-segment  = slug                        ; one sub-division segment
; NOTE: *(SLASH path-segment) allows arbitrary depth for works with 3+ structural levels
; e.g., summa-theologiae/iii/q75/a1 = work / part / question / article

; ── Institutions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
institution-path  = inst-type SLASH slug
inst-type         = slug                    ; a registered institution type
                                             ; (§3.7.2); [REV-05] formerly an
                                             ; enumeration in this grammar

; ── Relationship Types ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
rel-path    = rel-slug
rel-slug    = slug                          ; a registered relationship type
                                             ; (§3.8.2); [REV-05] formerly an
                                             ; enumeration in this grammar

; ============================================================================
; Validation notes (non-normative; see spec/03-domains.md for full discussion)
;
; 1. The canon-qualifier production makes cdcf:canon/cic1983/844/1 (paragraph)
;    and cdcf:canon/cic1983/230/authentic-interpretation/1994-11-11
;    unambiguous: a paragraph qualifier is 1*DIGIT; an authentic interpretation
;    begins with the fixed keyword "authentic-interpretation". No heuristic
;    parsing is required.
;
; 2. The work-path *(SLASH path-segment) production allows Thomas Aquinas's Summa
;    (three sub-levels: part/question/article) and other scholastic works of
;    arbitrary structural depth. It carries over the variable-depth production
;    of version 0.3.0's person-path, which version 0.5.0 withdraws (§3.6.1).
;    [REV-05] That production was written "[SLASH 1*path-segment]", which
;    concatenates segments without separators and so never matched
;    "summa-theologiae/iii/q75/a1"; the slash now precedes every segment.
;
; 3. All slug productions are restricted to lower-case ASCII (ALPHA = %x61-7A).
;    Upper-case characters are syntactically invalid in cdcf: identifiers,
;    except the fixed prefix of an opaque identifier. That prefix is written
;    as a hex literal (%x43.4E for "CN") because an ABNF quoted string is
;    case-insensitive under RFC 5234; it MUST appear in upper case. [REV-04]
;    The quoted domain names and keywords of this grammar match any case
;    under RFC 5234, but §2.3 rule 1 requires them in lower case; validators
;    therefore match quoted strings case-sensitively. [REV-05]
;
; 4. The iso-date production in canon-qualifier enforces ISO 8601 date format
;    for authentic interpretations, ensuring consistent machine parsing
;    across implementations.
;
; 5. The osis-book slug used in book-path and verse-path MUST be the exact,
;    lower-cased OSIS 2.1.1 book ID ("john", "matt"), matching the book
;    segment of the osisRef field byte-for-byte after case-folding.
;    Implementations MUST NOT introduce a second, undocumented abbreviation
;    scheme for the same book; version 0.3.0 shipped this defect (jn, mt) and
;    it was corrected in version 0.4.0. [REV-03] The former paths are not
;    aliases and are never redirected (§3.1). [REV-05]
;
; 6. The concept-path production is deliberately opaque (§2.6, §3.5): it
;    carries no linguistic content and MUST NOT be derived from, or assumed to
;    match, the concept's skos:notation. A client that has only a notation
;    string MUST resolve it via alias lookup (§4.9) before using the
;    identifier in a stored cross-reference. [REV-03] [REV-05]
;
; 7. concept-num admits exactly one spelling of each number: CN0007 is valid
;    and CN00007 is not; CN12345 is valid and CN012345 is not. Without this,
;    two strings could denote the same allocated number. [REV-05]
;
; 8. A segment that the grammar types as "slug" but whose values are
;    registered (code, inst-type, rel-slug) is valid only if the value is in
;    the registry; the tables in spec/03-domains.md are the registry's
;    initial content. Registering a value is a registry change, not a
;    grammar change (§6.6). [REV-05]
;
; 9. Test vectors for this grammar are in examples/test-vectors/ (valid.txt,
;    invalid.txt); CI asserts every valid vector conforms and every invalid
;    vector is rejected. [REV-05]
; ============================================================================
